.TH STS 1 "November 2026" "sts 3.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sts \- the Secure Talk System, end-to-end encrypted chat over MQTT
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sts \-c
.I FILE
.br
.B sts \-b
.I HOST
.B \-p
.I PORT
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B sts \-\-init
.br
.B sts \-\-passphrase
.I FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sts
is an IRC style group chat for the terminal. People who use the same MQTT
broker, the same topic prefix and the same room name (and password, if
any) are in the same room. Messages and files are encrypted and signed on
each computer: the broker, even a public one, only passes on data it
cannot read.
.PP
Settings come either all from a configuration
.IR FILE ,
or all from the command line; the two can't be mixed. With
.BR \-b " and " \-p ,
the other settings have defaults: nick = your login name, topic prefix
.BR sts ,
identity
.BR ~/.sts/identity.key ,
known peers
.BR ~/.sts/known_peers .
.PP
On a terminal,
.B sts
shows a full screen interface: messages on the left, the people of the
room on the right, a status bar and an input line. Otherwise (or with
.BR \-\-plain )
it prints one line per event and reads commands line by line, for
scripts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Read every setting from
.IR FILE .
No other option is accepted.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-broker " \fIHOST\fR"
MQTT broker host name.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIPORT\fR"
MQTT broker port: usually 1883 without TLS, 8883 with TLS.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-username " \fIUSER\fR, " \-P ", " \-\-password " \fIPASS\fR"
Broker account, if the broker asks for one. A password on the command line
can be seen by other users of the computer: prefer a configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-tls
Encrypt the connection to the broker. The certificate is checked against
the system's authorities, or
.BR \-\-ca\-file .
.TP
.BI \-\-ca\-file " FILE"
Certificate authorities to trust for TLS, for a broker with its own
authority.
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Don't check the broker's certificate. For tests only.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-topic\-prefix " \fISTR\fR"
MQTT topic prefix shared by the group (default
.BR sts ).
.TP
.BI \-\-keepalive " SECS"
Seconds between pings to the broker (30).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-nick " \fINICK\fR"
Nickname: letters, digits and
.B _ \- . [ ] { } ^ ` |
up to 24 characters.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-room " \fIROOM\fR[:\fIPASS\fR]"
Room to join, with its password if any. Can be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-identity " \fIFILE\fR"
Identity key, created on first start.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-known\-peers " \fIFILE\fR"
Fingerprints of the people met.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Line by line interface, no full screen.
.TP
.B \-\-log
Keep a chat log in
.BR ~/.sts/logs .
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-file\-size " SIZE"
Largest file sent or accepted, with an optional K, M or G (16M).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show protocol details.
.TP
.B \-\-init
Create a configuration file, step by step, and the identity key with an
optional passphrase.
.TP
.BI \-\-passphrase " FILE"
Protect the identity key
.I FILE
with a passphrase, change it, or remove it (empty passphrase).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
One
.B key = value
per line,
.B #
starts a comment. Relative paths are relative to the file,
.B ~/
is the home directory. Unknown keys and invalid values are errors, with
the line number.
.TP
.BR broker ", " port
The broker. Required.
.TP
.BR tls ", " tls_ca_file ", " tls_verify
TLS to the broker:
.BR yes / no ,
a CA file, and
.B tls_verify = no
to skip the check (tests only).
.TP
.BR username ", " password
Broker account, if needed.
.TP
.B topic_prefix
Shared by everyone who wants to talk. Required.
.TP
.BR nick ", " identity ", " known_peers
As the options above. Required.
.TP
.B room
.IR NAME " or " "NAME PASSWORD" ,
one line per room to join on start (up to 8).
.TP
.B rekey_interval
Seconds between key renewals, 0 for never (600).
.TP
.B keepalive
Seconds between pings (30).
.TP
.B ui
.BR auto ,
.B tui
(full screen) or
.B plain
.RB ( auto ).
.TP
.B max_file_size
Largest file sent or accepted, 1 byte to 64G (16M). Offers above it are
refused automatically.
.TP
.BR log ", " log_dir
.B log = yes
keeps a plain text log of each room in
.IR log_dir / ROOM .log
(default
.BR ~/.sts/logs ),
private messages included. The log is not encrypted.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI /join " ROOM " [ PASSWORD ]
Join or create a room, in a new window. Room names ignore case.
.TP
.BI /part " " [ ROOM ]
Leave the room.
.TP
.BI /msg " NICK TEXT"
Private message to someone in the room.
.TP
.BI /me " TEXT"
Action.
.TP
.BI /send " NICK FILE"
Offer a file to someone in the room.
.TP
.BI /accept " " [ N "] [" DIR ]
Accept file
.IR N ,
into
.B ~/Downloads
(your home directory if there is none) or
.IR DIR .
.TP
.BI /refuse " " [ N ]
Refuse file
.IR N .
.TP
.BI /cancel " N"
Stop transfer
.IR N ,
sending or receiving.
.TP
.B /files
Transfers in progress.
.TP
.BI /nick " NICK"
Change your nick.
.TP
.BR /who ", " /whois " \fINICK\fR"
The people in the room; someone's fingerprint.
.TP
.BR /trust " \fINICK\fR, " /untrust " \fINICK\fR"
Mark someone's key as verified, after comparing fingerprints outside of
the chat; remove the mark.
.TP
.B /fingerprint
Your own fingerprint.
.TP
.B /status
Connection, MQTT topics and encryption.
.TP
.B /rekey
Renew your keys now.
.TP
.BI /win " N"
Go to window
.IR N .
.TP
.BR /clear ", " /help ", " /quit
Clear the window, list the commands, leave every room and exit.
.SH KEYS
Alt\-1 to Alt\-9 go to a window, Ctrl\-N and Ctrl\-P to the next and
previous one. PgUp and PgDn scroll, Tab completes nicks and commands,
Up and Down browse the history, Ctrl\-A, Ctrl\-E, Ctrl\-U, Ctrl\-K and
Ctrl\-W edit the line, Ctrl\-C quits.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.sts/identity.key
Your identity key. Whoever has it can pass for you. Created readable by
you only; protect it with
.BR "sts \-\-passphrase" .
.TP
.B ~/.sts/known_peers
Fingerprints of the people met, and which ones you verified.
.TP
.B ~/.sts/sts.conf
The configuration made by
.BR "sts \-\-init" .
.TP
.B ~/.sts/logs/
Chat logs, with
.BR "log = yes" .
.SH SECURITY
Messages, private messages and files are end-to-end encrypted
(AES\-256\-GCM) and signed (ECDSA P\-256). Keys are renewed every 10
minutes and whenever someone joins or leaves: a newcomer can't read what
was said before, except in your first 10 seconds in a room.
.PP
Nicks can be taken by anyone, fingerprints can't. Compare fingerprints
outside of the chat before trusting someone, then use
.BR /trust :
.B sts
warns if that nick comes back with another key.
.PP
The broker can't read anything, but sees which topic is used, when, and
how much, and can refuse to pass messages on. A room without a password is
open to anyone who guesses its name. Whoever controls your computer can
read everything.
.SH EXAMPLES
A public broker without TLS:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sts \-b broker.emqx.io \-p 1883 \-t wonderland \-n kira \-r neotokyo
.EE
.RE
.PP
Your own mosquitto with TLS and its own authority:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sts \-b localhost \-p 8883 \-\-tls \-\-ca\-file ca.crt \\
    \-n kira \-r neotokyo
.EE
.RE
.PP
A message from a script:
.PP
.RS
.EX
(sleep 3; echo "deploy finished"; echo /quit) | sts \-c bot.conf
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mosquitto (8)
.PP
https://github.com/ifupauline/sts
